is: text of any script, numbers, null, and what is empty\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"annotationId\": \"ann-1\",\n        \"said\": \"two\\nlines, na\u00EFve, \u65E5\u672C\u8A9E\",\n        \"counted\": [1, 2.5, -3, { \"left\": null, \"right\": true }],\n        \"nothing\": { \"members\": {}, \"items\": [] }\n      },\n      \"shown\": {\n        \"annotationId\": \"ann-1\",\n        \"said\": \"two\\nlines, na\u00EFve, \u65E5\u672C\u8A9E\",\n        \"counted\": [1, 2.5, -3, { \"left\": null, \"right\": true }],\n        \"nothing\": { \"members\": {}, \"items\": [] }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"the empty payload is shown as it is\",\n      \"payload\": {},\n      \"shown\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"cloneToken, which is what an upload names the token a resource is cloned by\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"cloneToken\": \"clone-token-of-an-upload\", \"archiveOriginal\": true } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"cloneToken\": \"[withheld]\", \"archiveOriginal\": true } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"accessToken, a sign-in's access token as a program's record of it names it\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"accessToken\": \"access-token-in-a-record\", \"expiresAt\": \"2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"accessToken\": \"[withheld]\", \"expiresAt\": \"2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"access_token, the same as an issuer's reply names it: what says its kind and how long it lasts is shown\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"access_token\": \"access-token-in-a-reply\", \"token_type\": \"Bearer\", \"expires_in\": 300 } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"access_token\": \"[withheld]\", \"token_type\": \"Bearer\", \"expires_in\": 300 } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"refreshToken, a sign-in's refresh token as the sign-in store names it\",\n      \"payload\": { \"metadata\": { \"refreshToken\": \"refresh-token-in-a-store\", \"issuer\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"metadata\": { \"refreshToken\": \"[withheld]\", \"issuer\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"refresh_token, the same as an issuer and a refresh grant name it: the grant's kind, whose value is the name, is shown\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": \"refresh-token-in-a-grant\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"apiKey, an inference provider's key as a knowledge base's configuration names it, among an agent's parameters\",\n      \"payload\": { \"generator\": { \"@type\": \"Software\", \"name\": \"A model\", \"parameters\": { \"temperature\": 0.2, \"apiKey\": \"provider-key-in-a-configuration\" } } },\n      \"shown\": { \"generator\": { \"@type\": \"Software\", \"name\": \"A model\", \"parameters\": { \"temperature\": 0.2, \"apiKey\": \"[withheld]\" } } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"api_key, the same as a Python program names it\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"provider\": \"anthropic\", \"base_url\": \"https://api.example\", \"api_key\": \"provider-key-in-a-program\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"provider\": \"anthropic\", \"base_url\": \"https://api.example\", \"api_key\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"clientSecret, a service's secret at its issuer as a program's record of it names it\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"issuer\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\", \"clientId\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"clientSecret\": \"client-secret-in-a-record\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"issuer\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\", \"clientId\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"clientSecret\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"client_secret, the same as the grant that spends it names it\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"grant_type\": \"client_credentials\", \"client_id\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"client_secret\": \"client-secret-in-a-grant\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"grant_type\": \"client_credentials\", \"client_id\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"client_secret\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"secret: a member of that name holds one, whatever it is the secret of\",\n      \"payload\": { \"metadata\": { \"client\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"secret\": \"a-secret\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"metadata\": { \"client\": \"xynolog-worker\", \"secret\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"password: a member of that name holds one, whatever it opens\",\n      \"payload\": { \"params\": { \"user\": \"xynolog\", \"password\": \"a-password\" } },\n      \"shown\": { \"params\": { \"user\": \"xynolog\", \"password\": \"[withheld]\" } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"authorization, the header a credential is sent under, among the headers of a request a result repeats\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"authorization\": \"Bearer a-token-in-a-header\", \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"authorization\": \"[withheld]\", \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"Authorization, the same header in its other spelling\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer another-token-in-a-header\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" } } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"[withheld]\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" } } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"x-api-key, the header one inference provider takes its key under\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"x-api-key\": \"provider-key-in-a-header\", \"anthropic-version\": \"2023-06-01\" } } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"x-api-key\": \"[withheld]\", \"anthropic-version\": \"2023-06-01\" } } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"x-goog-api-key, the header another takes its key under\",\n      \"payload\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"x-goog-api-key\": \"another-provider-key-in-a-header\", \"x-goog-api-client\": \"a-client/1.0\" } } },\n      \"shown\": { \"result\": { \"headers\": { \"x-goog-api-key\": \"[withheld]\", \"x-goog-api-client\": \"a-client/1.0\" } } }\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a name that only contains one of the names is another name, and is shown: the member that names the environment variable a credential is read from, an issuer's endpoint, who a request is authenticated as, and where authorization is had\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"engines\": [{ \"baseUrl\": \"https://api.example\", \"apiKeyEnv\": \"PROVIDER_API_KEY\" }],\n        \"broker\": { \"passwordEnv\": \"BROKER_PASSWORD\" },\n        \"signIn\": { \"tokenEndpoint\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb/token\" },\n        \"status\": { \"authenticatedAs\": \"did:web:example.org:users:alice\", \"authorization_servers\": [\"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\"] }\n      },\n      \"shown\": {\n        \"engines\": [{ \"baseUrl\": \"https://api.example\", \"apiKeyEnv\": \"PROVIDER_API_KEY\" }],\n        \"broker\": { \"passwordEnv\": \"BROKER_PASSWORD\" },\n        \"signIn\": { \"tokenEndpoint\": \"https://issuer.example/realms/kb/token\" },\n        \"status\": { \"authenticatedAs\": \"did:web:example.org:users:alice\", \"authorization_servers\": [\"https://issuer.example/realms/kb\"] }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const string OwnerOnly = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"AUTHORITY for how a writer of tokens.json keeps <stateDir> and its files to its owner (README.md, Where it is), and how the launcher keeps its state home and its own files there: a mode and an access list for a directory, and a mode and an access list for a file, which every writer gives what it makes. A mode or a list restated in each language is one that differs in one of them unseen. Go: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/go/owneronly_gen.go and the launcher's cli/internal/launcher/owneronly_gen.go. Python: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/python/sdk/src/xynolog/_owner_only_table.py. Rust: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/rust/sdk/src/generated/owner_only.rs. Kotlin: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/generated/kotlin/xynolog/signin/OwnerOnlyTable.kt. Swift: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/swift/sdk/Sources/Xynolog/Generated/Models.swift. C#: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/csharp/sdk/src/Xynolog/Generated/ProtocolTables.g.cs. TypeScript: the consumer-owned generator writes @xynolog/core's src/sign-in.ts. Haskell: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/haskell/sdk/generated/Xynolog/Internal/Generated/xynolog_store_policy.h. OCaml: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/ocaml/sdk/lib/store_policy.ml and its storage probe's sdk/ocaml/sdk/probes/store_policy.ml.\",\n  \"directoryMode\": {\n    \"value\": \"0700\",\n    \"docs\": \"The directory's mode, in octal, on a system that has modes: its owner reads, writes and enters it, and nobody else does.\"\n  },\n  \"fileMode\": {\n    \"value\": \"0600\",\n    \"docs\": \"The mode, in octal, on a system that has modes, that a writer makes tokens.json's temporary file and its lock with, and the launcher its own files in its state home: its owner reads and writes each, and nobody else does.\"\n  },\n  \"directoryAccessList\": {\n    \"value\": \"D:PAI(A;OICI;FA;;;{owner})(A;OICI;FA;;;SY)(A;OICI;FA;;;BA)\",\n    \"docs\": \"The directory's access list on Windows, where a mode keeps nobody out, in SDDL, with `{owner}` where the SID of the user the writer runs as goes (its process token's user): full access for that user, the system and the administrators, and nobody else. It is handed down to everything made in the directory, and protected, so nothing is inherited from above.\"\n  },\n  \"fileAccessList\": {\n    \"value\": \"D:PAI(A;;FA;;;{owner})(A;;FA;;;SY)(A;;FA;;;BA)\",\n    \"docs\": \"A file's access list on Windows, which the launcher gives each file it keeps to its owner, in SDDL, with `{owner}` where the SID of the user it runs as goes: the directory's list, with nothing handed down, since a file has nothing beneath it. Full access for that user, the system and the administrators, and nobody else, protected, so nothing is inherited from above.\"\n  }\n}\n";
    internal const string OAuth = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"AUTHORITY for how a Xynolog client presents itself to the issuer a knowledge base trusts. The realm registers these clients (the launcher writes the registration), and every SDK and the launcher sign in as them: a client id restated in each language is a sign-in that fails in one of them the day the registration changes. TypeScript: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/typescript/core/src/oauth-clients.ts. Rust: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/rust/sdk/src/generated/oauth_clients.rs. Python: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/python/sdk/src/xynolog/oauth_clients.py. Go: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/go/oauthclients_gen.go, which the launcher reads too. Kotlin: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/generated/kotlin/xynolog/signin/OAuthClients.kt.\",\n  \"clients\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"browser\",\n      \"id\": \"xynolog-browser\",\n      \"docs\": \"An application a person uses: the authorization-code grant with PKCE (RFC 7636), at a redirect address the registration lists.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"script\",\n      \"id\": \"xynolog-cli\",\n      \"docs\": \"A process with no browser of its own, and the launcher: the device authorization grant (RFC 8628).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"value\": \"openid email profile offline_access\",\n    \"docs\": \"What every sign-in asks for. `offline_access` asks for a refresh token that outlives the issuer's own browser session: a session with a knowledge base is renewed for weeks, not minutes.\"\n  }\n}\n";
    internal const string ClientAssertion = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"How a service account proves itself with a key instead of a secret: OpenID Connect's private_key_jwt, the client assertion of RFC 7523 \u00A72.2. The account holds an RSA private key; its issuer holds the public half, registered on the account's client. For each client-credentials grant the account signs a fresh JWT with RS256: its header names the key by its JWK thumbprint (RFC 7638: the SHA-256 of the key's required members `e`, `kty` and `n`, in that order, with no whitespace, base64url without padding), and its claims are `iss` and `sub` the client id, `aud` the issuer's token endpoint, `jti` a value never sent twice, `iat` when it is made and `exp` `lifetimeSeconds` after. The grant posts the form's fields and no others: the client id is the assertion's `sub`, and no secret is sent. A JSON object here is compared as JSON, member order aside. Every implementation that signs such an assertion runs every case.\",\n  \"runBy\": {\n    \"haskell\": [\"sdk/haskell/sdk/test/ClientAssertionCases.hs\"],\n    \"csharp\": [\"sdk/csharp/sdk/tests/Xynolog.Tests/ServiceTokenTests.cs\"],\n    \"swift\": [\"sdk/swift/sdk/Tests/XynologTests/IssuerTests.swift\"],\n    \"python\": [\"sdk/python/sdk/tests/test_client_assertion_cases.py\"],\n    \"typescript\": [\n      \"sdk/typescript/core/src/__tests__/client-assertion-cases.test.ts\",\n      \"sdk/typescript/core/src/__tests__/key-credential.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"rust\": [\"sdk/rust/http-transport/tests/client_assertion_cases.rs\"],\n    \"go\": [\"sdk/go/clientassertion_test.go\"],\n    \"kotlin\": [\"sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/test/kotlin/xynolog/http/ClientAssertionCasesTest.kt\"],\n    \"ocaml\": [\"sdk/ocaml/sdk/test/sign_in.ml\"]\n  },\n  \"form\": [\"grant_type\", \"client_assertion_type\", \"client_assertion\"],\n  \"grantType\": \"client_credentials\",\n  \"assertionType\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer\",\n  \"lifetimeSeconds\": 60,\n  \"thumbprints\": [\n    {\n      \"why\": \"RFC 7638 \u00A73.1's own example key and thumbprint\",\n      \"jwk\": {\n        \"kty\": \"RSA\",\n        \"n\": \"0vx7agoebGcQSuuPiLJXZptN9nndrQmbXEps2aiAFbWhM78LhWx4cbbfAAtVT86zwu1RK7aPFFxuhDR1L6tSoc_BJECPebWKRXjBZCiFV4n3oknjhMstn64tZ_2W-5JsGY4Hc5n9yBXArwl93lqt7_RN5w6Cf0h4QyQ5v-65YGjQR0_FDW2QvzqY368QQMicAtaSqzs8KJZgnYb9c7d0zgdAZHzu6qMQvRL5hajrn1n91CbOpbISD08qNLyrdkt-bFTWhAI4vMQFh6WeZu0fM4lFd2NcRwr3XPksINHaQ-G_xBniIqbw0Ls1jF44-csFCur-kEgU8awapJzKnqDKgw\",\n        \"e\": \"AQAB\"\n      },\n      \"thumbprint\": \"NzbLsXh8uDCcd-6MNwXF4W_7noWXFZAfHkxZsRGC9Xs\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a worker's assertion at a launcher-run Keycloak, its key RFC 7638's example\",\n      \"jwk\": {\n        \"kty\": \"RSA\",\n        \"n\": \"0vx7agoebGcQSuuPiLJXZptN9nndrQmbXEps2aiAFbWhM78LhWx4cbbfAAtVT86zwu1RK7aPFFxuhDR1L6tSoc_BJECPebWKRXjBZCiFV4n3oknjhMstn64tZ_2W-5JsGY4Hc5n9yBXArwl93lqt7_RN5w6Cf0h4QyQ5v-65YGjQR0_FDW2QvzqY368QQMicAtaSqzs8KJZgnYb9c7d0zgdAZHzu6qMQvRL5hajrn1n91CbOpbISD08qNLyrdkt-bFTWhAI4vMQFh6WeZu0fM4lFd2NcRwr3XPksINHaQ-G_xBniIqbw0Ls1jF44-csFCur-kEgU8awapJzKnqDKgw\",\n        \"e\": \"AQAB\"\n      },\n      \"clientId\": \"xynolog-worker-alice-laptop\",\n      \"tokenEndpoint\": \"http://localhost:8080/realms/xynolog/protocol/openid-connect/token\",\n      \"issuedAt\": 1798761600,\n      \"jti\": \"6f1d3c2a9b8e4f70a5d2c1b0e9f8a7d6\",\n      \"header\": { \"alg\": \"RS256\", \"kid\": \"NzbLsXh8uDCcd-6MNwXF4W_7noWXFZAfHkxZsRGC9Xs\" },\n      \"claims\": {\n        \"iss\": \"xynolog-worker-alice-laptop\",\n        \"sub\": \"xynolog-worker-alice-laptop\",\n        \"aud\": \"http://localhost:8080/realms/xynolog/protocol/openid-connect/token\",\n        \"jti\": \"6f1d3c2a9b8e4f70a5d2c1b0e9f8a7d6\",\n        \"iat\": 1798761600,\n        \"exp\": 1798761660\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const string Principals = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"How the gateway names the principals it acts for, under the knowledge base's domain (its committed `site.domain`). Every principal is named by the subject its issuer asserted, under the kind its token says it is: an agent's account carries the claim `kind` holding `agent`, and any other is a person's. A person is `did:web:{domain}:users:{subject}` and an agent `did:web:{domain}:agents:{subject}`, where the subject is the value of the claim `identity.subjectClaim` names. Every part of a DID after the domain is percent-encoded as ECMAScript's encodeURIComponent does: each UTF-8 byte of a character other than A\u2013Z a\u2013z 0\u20139 - _ . ! ~ * ' ( ) becomes %XX in uppercase hex; the domain is written as it is. Every implementation that names these principals runs every case and fails on a difference, and a running gateway is held to every case too.\",\n  \"runBy\": {\n    \"ocaml\": [\"sdk/ocaml/sdk/test/closure_behavior.ml\"],\n    \"haskell\": [\"sdk/haskell/sdk/test/IdentityCases.hs\"],\n    \"csharp\": [\"sdk/csharp/sdk/tests/Xynolog.Tests/IdentityTests.cs\"],\n    \"swift\": [\"sdk/swift/sdk/Tests/XynologTests/SessionTablesTests.swift\"],\n    \"rust\": [\n      \"sdk/rust/sdk/tests/tables.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"python\": [\n      \"sdk/python/sdk/tests/test_identity.py\"\n    ],\n    \"go\": [\n      \"sdk/go/identity_test.go\"\n    ],\n    \"conformance\": [\n      \"conformance/gateway/tokens.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"kotlin\": [\n      \"sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/test/kotlin/xynolog/identity/IdentityTest.kt\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"absent\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"No TypeScript code names a principal: the gateway, in Rust, mints every DID it acts for.\"\n  },\n  \"person\": \"did:web:{domain}:users:{subject}\",\n  \"people\": [\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a subject of letters and digits is itself\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"alice\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:alice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a UUID subject is itself\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"3f1c2e0a-9b7d-4c1e-8a2f-6d5b4c3a2e10\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:3f1c2e0a-9b7d-4c1e-8a2f-6d5b4c3a2e10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"an email-shaped subject encodes its @\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"alice@example.org\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:alice%40example.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a colon in the subject is encoded, so it cannot split the DID\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"google-oauth2:104859221\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:google-oauth2%3A104859221\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a slash in the subject is encoded\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"tenant/alice\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:tenant%2Falice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a space is %20\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"Alice Smith\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:Alice%20Smith\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a character outside ASCII is its UTF-8 bytes, each percent-encoded\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"jos\u00E9\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:jos%C3%A9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"the characters encodeURIComponent leaves alone stay as they are\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"a-b_c.d!e~f*g'h(i)j\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:users:a-b_c.d!e~f*g'h(i)j\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent\": \"did:web:{domain}:agents:{subject}\",\n  \"agents\": [\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a subject of letters, digits and hyphens is itself\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"xynolog-worker-local\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:agents:xynolog-worker-local\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a UUID subject, as an issuer names a client's own account, is itself\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"7c1f3d2a-5b6e-4f80-9a1b-2c3d4e5f6a7b\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:agents:7c1f3d2a-5b6e-4f80-9a1b-2c3d4e5f6a7b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a colon in the subject is encoded, so it cannot split the DID\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"service-account:worker\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:agents:service-account%3Aworker\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"an email-shaped subject encodes its @\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"worker@example.org\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:agents:worker%40example.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"why\": \"a slash in the subject is encoded\",\n      \"domain\": \"example.org:test-kb\",\n      \"subject\": \"tenant/worker\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:example.org:test-kb:agents:tenant%2Fworker\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const string MediaTypes = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"AUTHORITY for the media types a knowledge base admits, and what the system can do with each. A row's `mediaType` is a member of the `SupportedMediaType` schema, and every member has exactly one row: the generators refuse a registry and an enum that disagree. Admission is membership: every row is storable, nameable and uploadable. The capabilities say what more there is. `render` is the viewer a reader mounts (`none`: metadata and a download). `anchoring` is the annotation model: character-offset text selectors, or spatial geometry. `textSource` is where a type's text comes from: decoded from its own bytes, derived by reading them (`pdf-text-layer`), or nowhere. `authorable` types are offered where a person writes a resource, and a clone keeps its source's type only when it is one. `generatable` types are ones the generation worker can produce. `application/pdf` is one because the worker compiles Typst the model writes. Every row whose `render` and `anchoring` are `none` is stored, named and downloadable and nothing more: a deliberate admission, promoted by editing its row. `extension` is the one a stored name takes, with its dot. ROW ORDER MATTERS: two types that share an extension (.xml, .yaml, .js, .ts, .webm) resolve, from the extension, to the first row that states it. The video rows are before the audio rows so that .webm is video. `extensionAliases` are other spellings of an extension a file may carry, each with the extension a row states that it is read as. TypeScript: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/typescript/core/src/media-types.ts. Rust: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/rust/sdk/src/generated/media_types.rs, `xynolog::media_types`. Go: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/go/mediatypes/registry_gen.go, which is committed and checked for drift in CI. Python: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/python/sdk/src/xynolog/media_types_table.py, which is committed and checked for drift in CI too. Kotlin: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/generated/kotlin/xynolog/mediatypes/MediaTypesTable.kt. The rules read from this table (which format a clone takes, the name content is stored under) are held in every SDK by cases.json.\",\n  \"render\": [\"text\", \"image\", \"pdf\", \"none\"],\n  \"anchoring\": [\"text-selector\", \"spatial\", \"none\"],\n  \"textSource\": [\"decode\", \"pdf-text-layer\", \"none\"],\n  \"extensionAliases\": {\n    \".markdown\": \".md\",\n    \".htm\": \".html\",\n    \".jpeg\": \".jpg\",\n    \".yml\": \".yaml\"\n  },\n  \"mediaTypes\": [\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/markdown\", \"extension\": \".md\", \"label\": \"Markdown\", \"render\": \"text\", \"anchoring\": \"text-selector\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": true, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": true },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/plain\", \"extension\": \".txt\", \"label\": \"Plain Text\", \"render\": \"text\", \"anchoring\": \"text-selector\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": true, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": true },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/html\", \"extension\": \".html\", \"label\": \"HTML\", \"render\": \"text\", \"anchoring\": \"text-selector\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": true, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/json\", \"extension\": \".json\", \"label\": \"JSON\", \"render\": \"text\", \"anchoring\": \"text-selector\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"image/png\", \"extension\": \".png\", \"label\": \"PNG image\", \"render\": \"image\", \"anchoring\": \"spatial\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"image/jpeg\", \"extension\": \".jpg\", \"label\": \"JPEG image\", \"render\": \"image\", \"anchoring\": \"spatial\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/pdf\", \"extension\": \".pdf\", \"label\": \"PDF\", \"render\": \"pdf\", \"anchoring\": \"spatial\", \"textSource\": \"pdf-text-layer\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": true },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/css\", \"extension\": \".css\", \"label\": \"CSS\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/csv\", \"extension\": \".csv\", \"label\": \"CSV\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/xml\", \"extension\": \".xml\", \"label\": \"XML\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/xml\", \"extension\": \".xml\", \"label\": \"XML\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/yaml\", \"extension\": \".yaml\", \"label\": \"YAML\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/x-yaml\", \"extension\": \".yaml\", \"label\": \"YAML\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/javascript\", \"extension\": \".js\", \"label\": \"JavaScript\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/javascript\", \"extension\": \".js\", \"label\": \"JavaScript\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-typescript\", \"extension\": \".ts\", \"label\": \"TypeScript\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/typescript\", \"extension\": \".ts\", \"label\": \"TypeScript\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-python\", \"extension\": \".py\", \"label\": \"Python source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-java\", \"extension\": \".java\", \"label\": \"Java source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-c\", \"extension\": \".c\", \"label\": \"C source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-c++\", \"extension\": \".cpp\", \"label\": \"C++ source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-csharp\", \"extension\": \".cs\", \"label\": \"C# source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-go\", \"extension\": \".go\", \"label\": \"Go source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-rust\", \"extension\": \".rs\", \"label\": \"Rust source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-ruby\", \"extension\": \".rb\", \"label\": \"Ruby source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-php\", \"extension\": \".php\", \"label\": \"PHP source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-swift\", \"extension\": \".swift\", \"label\": \"Swift source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-kotlin\", \"extension\": \".kt\", \"label\": \"Kotlin source\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"text/x-shell\", \"extension\": \".sh\", \"label\": \"Shell script\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"decode\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/msword\", \"extension\": \".doc\", \"label\": \"Word document (legacy)\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\", \"extension\": \".docx\", \"label\": \"Word document\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.ms-excel\", \"extension\": \".xls\", \"label\": \"Excel spreadsheet (legacy)\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\", \"extension\": \".xlsx\", \"label\": \"Excel spreadsheet\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.ms-powerpoint\", \"extension\": \".ppt\", \"label\": \"PowerPoint presentation (legacy)\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation\", \"extension\": \".pptx\", \"label\": \"PowerPoint presentation\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/zip\", \"extension\": \".zip\", \"label\": \"ZIP archive\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/gzip\", \"extension\": \".gz\", \"label\": \"Gzip archive\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/x-tar\", \"extension\": \".tar\", \"label\": \"TAR archive\", \"render\": \"none\", \"anchoring\": \"none\", \"textSource\": \"none\", \"authorable\": false, \"uploadable\": true, \"generatable\": false },\n    { \"mediaType\": \"application/x-7z-compressed\", \"extensio