\",\n        \"iso-2022-cn-ext\",\n        \"iso-2022-kr\",\n        \"replacement\"\n      ],\n      \"refused\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const string CacheRefresh = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"AUTHORITY for what a Xynolog client asks again for, and when. A client's live queries answer from a cache (contract/CACHE-SEMANTICS.md); this table says what each event on the bus, and the reopening of a dropped stream, does to it. `queries` names the live queries: the operation of the registry each one `asks`, or the GET of the gateway's API it `reads` when its answer grows with a document, and what one is kept `per` (a resource, an annotation, a set of filters; absent, the knowledge base has one). Each one's `value` is the schema of what its cache holds for a key: a component, or a member within one, named member by member (`#/properties/\u2026`). What a query shows may be a view of its value: `annotations` shows its value's annotations, and `engines` each engine joined with the limits reported for it. A query marked `persisted` is one whose answers a client keeps across its lives, for the person signed in, under its name (specs/src/session/stored.json, `cacheKeyPrefix`), each kept value its `value`; every other is held in memory alone. A persisted query's `value` is a component, or a member that is all the component holding it requires, so that a value kept by one client is held to the component when another reads it back. Every SDK's type for each query's value is generated from `value`, or held to it by a test. `refresh` has a row per trigger: `on` is a channel of specs/src/bus/registry.json; or `reopened`, the stream open again after a drop (never after a handoff, which misses nothing); or `unreadable`, an event on one of the table's channels that cannot be read. A row `refetches` queries (asks again, keeping the value shown meanwhile), `writes` those whose new value the event itself carries, and `removes` those whose entity the event says is gone, which then fail as `bus.not-found`. `reach` says which keys: `subject`, the resource the event names and, of that resource's annotations, the one it names, or each the client holds when it names none; or `held`, every key the client holds. `names` says where in the event (the frame's payload) a `subject` row finds them: the way to the `resource` (a ResourceId) and to the `annotation` (an AnnotationId), the names of the members it is within and its own joined by dots, as a frame's refusal names a member. `carries` is the way to the value the row `writes` (an Annotation). A way names none where its member, or a member it passes through, is absent or null. A member it passes through that is present and is no object, the member it ends at present and not of its type, and a frame its channel's reading refuses each make the event `unreadable`, whose row applies in its place. `when` splits a channel whose events come two ways: `enriched`, when the member its `enriched` row `carries` is present and not null, and `unenriched` otherwise. the consumer-owned generator holds every way to the schema of its channel's events. A client acts only on keys it holds (B20). TypeScript: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/typescript/core/src/cache-refresh.ts. conformance/sdk builds a live case from every row.\",\n  \"queries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"resource\",\n      \"per\": \"resource\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:resource-requested\",\n      \"persisted\": true,\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/ResourceDescriptor.json\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"A resource's description.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"annotations\",\n      \"per\": \"resource\",\n      \"reads\": \"GET /resources/{id}/annotations\",\n      \"persisted\": true,\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/GetAnnotationsResponse.json\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The annotations of a resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"annotation\",\n      \"per\": \"annotation\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:annotation-requested\",\n      \"persisted\": true,\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/Annotation.json\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"One annotation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"events\",\n      \"per\": \"resource\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:events-requested\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/GetEventsResponse.json#/properties/events\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The recorded history of a resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"referencedBy\",\n      \"per\": \"resource\",\n      \"asks\": \"gather:referenced-by-requested\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/GetReferencedByResponse.json#/properties/referencedBy\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The annotations elsewhere that refer to a resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"resources\",\n      \"per\": \"filters\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:resources-requested\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/ListResourcesResponse.json\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"A list of resources, one per set of filters asked for. It is a query's answer, kept fresh by what every client hears and by the events of the resources whose scope the client holds, and by nothing else: a resource archived, unarchived or retagged elsewhere, by someone else, does not refresh it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"matchedResources\",\n      \"per\": \"filters\",\n      \"asks\": \"match:resources-requested\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/MatchResourcesResponse.json\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The resources a text search found, one per search and set of filters asked for. A query's answer like `resources`, and kept fresh by the same events and no others.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"entityTypes\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:entity-types-requested\",\n      \"persisted\": true,\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/GetEntityTypesResponse.json#/properties/entityTypes\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The knowledge base's entity types.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tagSchemas\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:tag-schemas-requested\",\n      \"persisted\": true,\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/GetTagSchemasResponse.json#/properties/tagSchemas\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The knowledge base's tag schemas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"engines\",\n      \"asks\": \"browse:engines-requested\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/BrowseEnginesResult.json#/properties/response/properties/engines\"\n      },\n      \"docs\": \"The knowledge base's engines, joined with the limits each inference key holder reports: asking again asks every `<flow>:limits-requested` operation of the registry again too.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"refresh\": [\n    {\n      \"on\": \"reopened\",\n      \"reach\": \"held\",\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\",\n        \"resource\",\n        \"entityTypes\",\n        \"tagSchemas\",\n        \"engines\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"The stream is open again after a drop. Events every client hears carry no position, so the ones published meanwhile are lost and nothing replays them: the client asks again for everything they feed. What a resource's own scope feeds needs nothing here: its events are replayed from where the client left off, or `bus:resume-gap` says they could not be.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"unreadable\",\n      \"reach\": \"held\",\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"annotation\",\n        \"events\",\n        \"referencedBy\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\",\n        \"entityTypes\",\n        \"tagSchemas\",\n        \"engines\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A frame on a channel of this table that its reading refuses, or one a member of which the row names is present and is not what it names: something changed and nothing says what, so every key held is asked for again, as after a gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"bus:resume-gap\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"scope\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"annotation\",\n        \"resource\",\n        \"events\",\n        \"referencedBy\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"The gateway could not replay what a scope missed: everything held of that resource, and of its annotations, is asked for again.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:added\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An annotation was added to the resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:removed\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\",\n        \"annotation\": \"payload.annotationId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"removes\": [\n        \"annotation\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An annotation was removed from the resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:delete-ok\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"annotation\": \"response.annotationId\"\n      },\n      \"removes\": [\n        \"annotation\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"The reply to this client's own deletion: the annotation is gone whether or not the client holds the scope that would tell it so.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:body-updated\",\n      \"when\": \"enriched\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\",\n        \"annotation\": \"annotation.id\"\n      },\n      \"carries\": \"annotation\",\n      \"writes\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"annotation\"\n      ],\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An annotation's body changed, and the event carries the annotation as it now is.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:body-updated\",\n      \"when\": \"unenriched\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\",\n        \"annotation\": \"payload.annotationId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"annotation\",\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An annotation's body changed, and the event could not say what it now is.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:entity-tag-added\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"resource\",\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An entity tag was added to the resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:entity-tag-removed\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"annotations\",\n        \"resource\",\n        \"events\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An entity tag was removed from the resource.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:archived\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"The resource was archived, which its description states and lists filter on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"mark:unarchived\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"The resource was unarchived.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"yield:created\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A resource was created.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"yield:updated\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A resource was updated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"yield:cloned\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A resource was created as a clone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"yield:moved\",\n      \"names\": {\n        \"resource\": \"resourceId\"\n      },\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"resource\",\n        \"resources\",\n        \"matchedResources\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A resource was renamed or moved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"frame:entity-type-added\",\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"entityTypes\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"An entity type was added to the knowledge base.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"on\": \"frame:tag-schema-added\",\n      \"refetches\": [\n        \"tagSchemas\"\n      ],\n      \"docs\": \"A tag schema was added to the knowledge base.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const string Stored = "{\n  \"$comment\": \"AUTHORITY for what a registry of knowledge bases keeps in a SessionStorage, and what the sessions it makes keep there: the key each thing is kept under, the shape of a knowledge base's stored session, the shape of a resource open in one, the shape of a sign-in by a page redirect that is under way, and what a client keeps of its queries and of its stream. A registry in any SDK finds what one in another wrote, over one storage, only if every SDK says these alike. WHO HOLDS IT. TypeScript states it by hand in sdk/typescript/sdk/src/session/storage.ts, oauth.ts and open-resource.ts, held by sdk/typescript/sdk/src/session/__tests__/stored-table.test.ts and oauth.test.ts. Rust in sdk/rust/sdk/src/session/stored.rs and open_resource.rs, held by sdk/rust/sdk/tests/tables.rs, and in sdk/rust/http-transport/src/oauth.rs, held by sdk/rust/http-transport/tests/sign_in.rs. Go in sdk/go/registry/stored.go and openresource.go, held by sdk/go/registry/stored_test.go, and in sdk/go/authorization.go and storage.go, held by sdk/go/stored_test.go. Kotlin in sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/main/kotlin/xynolog/registry/Stored.kt and Open.kt and xynolog/http/Authorization.kt, held by sdk/kotlin/sdk/src/test/kotlin/xynolog/registry/StoredTest.kt and xynolog/http/AuthorizationTest.kt. Swift in sdk/swift/sdk/Sources/Xynolog/Registry/Stored.swift, OpenResources.swift and RedirectSignIn.swift, held by sdk/swift/sdk/Tests/XynologTests/RegistryTablesTests.swift and IssuerTests.swift; the consumer-owned generator writes its stored session, HeldSignIn, of `storedSession` into sdk/swift/sdk/Sources/Xynolog/Generated/Models.swift. C# reads the table, which the consumer-owned generator embeds in sdk/csharp/sdk/src/Xynolog/Generated/ProtocolTables.g.cs, in sdk/csharp/sdk/src/Xynolog/Registry/RegistryStorage.cs, where it states the open resource, and states the pending sign-in in sdk/csharp/sdk/src/Xynolog/Authorization/RedirectSignIn.cs, held by sdk/csharp/sdk/tests/Xynolog.Tests/RegistryTests.cs. Python: the consumer-owned generator writes sdk/python/sdk/src/xynolog/stored.py, and sdk/python/sdk/tests/test_registry_http.py holds the pending sign-in of sdk/python/sdk/src/xynolog/http/oauth.py. Haskell: the consumer-owned generator writes its keys and prefixes (sdk/haskell/sdk/generated/Xynolog/Internal/Generated/Stored.hs) and its stored session, pending sign-in and open resource (Models/StoredSession.hs, PendingAuthorization.hs and OpenResource.hs beside it) from the table. What a client keeps of its queries and of its stream (`wholeKey`, `cacheDocument`, `lastEventIds`) every SDK holds by running specs/src/session/cache-cases.json against its own persister: what it writes, and what it keeps of what another wrote. READING IT. `keys` are the fixed keys, each named as specs/src/client/surface.json names its constant. A knowledge base's session is kept under `sessionKeyPrefix` followed by the knowledge base's id, and `storedSession` is what is kept there, as JSON: a flat object schema whose every member is text. `lastEventIdKeyPrefix` and `cacheKeyPrefix` begin the keys of what a session keeps of its stream and its queries for one person, as each one's `docs` says, and each one's `example` is one key worked out from a knowledge base's id, a person's did and, for a query, its name. The queries a client keeps across a restart are those specs/src/client/refresh.json marks `persisted`, each kept as a `cacheDocument` under `cacheKeyPrefix`, its entries' values what the query's `value` there says its cache holds. An entry's key is a resource's id for a query `per` resource, an annotation's id for one `per` annotation, and `wholeKey` for one per nothing; a query per filters is not kept. A load keeps nothing of a document whose structure is not `cacheDocument`'s (not JSON, not an object, of another version, its `entries` not a list, or an entry not a key, a value and a stamp), and skips an entry whose key or value is not what its query keeps. A load of `lastEventIds` skips a pair that is not a resource's id and a PersistedEventId, and keeps none of a value that is no object. `pendingAuthorization` is what is kept under `pendingAuthorizationKey`, and `openResource` each entry of a list kept under `openResourcesByKbKey`, as JSON; a member either does not require is not written when there is none.\",\n  \"keys\": [\n    {\n      \"member\": \"knowledgeBasesKey\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.knowledgeBases\",\n      \"docs\": \"The registered knowledge bases: a JSON list of KnowledgeBase (components/schemas/KnowledgeBase.json).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"member\": \"activeKey\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.activeKnowledgeBaseId\",\n      \"docs\": \"The id of the active knowledge base. Nothing is kept under it while none is active.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"member\": \"openResourcesByKbKey\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.openResourcesByKb\",\n      \"docs\": \"What is open in each knowledge base: a JSON object from a knowledge base's id to the list of its open resources, each an `openResource`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"member\": \"lastViewedResourceByKbKey\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.lastViewedResourceByKb\",\n      \"docs\": \"Where the person was in each knowledge base: a JSON object from a knowledge base's id to the id of the resource last viewed in it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"member\": \"pendingAuthorizationKey\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.pendingAuthorization\",\n      \"docs\": \"A sign-in by a page redirect that is under way: what it remembers across the trip to the issuer and back. It is taken when the sign-in completes, so a callback that is replayed finds nothing to complete.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sessionKeyPrefix\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"xynolog.session.\",\n    \"docs\": \"A knowledge base's stored session is kept under this followed by the knowledge base's id.\"\n  },\n  \"lastEventIdKeyPrefix\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"xynolog.lastEventId.\",\n    \"docs\": \"Where a knowledge base's stream was, for one person, is kept under this followed by the knowledge base's id, a dot and the person's key: the unpadded base64url SHA-256 of the UTF-8 of the did the gateway answers for the person's token (components/schemas/UserResponse.json), never the did itself. What is kept is `lastEventIds`. It is written in the same call as a write of one of the caches kept beside it, and only while every kept cache has no fetch in flight and owes no save, and the refresher owes no refetch (a window of B19, contract/CACHE-SEMANTICS.md, that holds an invalidation it has not yet run); so it never leads them. Its own write is never a reason to write a cache. At disposal this is read once, before any kept cache or the refresher is disposed. Nothing is kept for a token whose person the gateway has not named, and forgetting the knowledge base's stored sign-in, however it is forgotten, deletes it.\",\n    \"example\": {\n      \"kbId\": \"kb-a\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:kb.example.org:users:jo%40example.org\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.lastEventId.kb-a.gqB898gk4Ww_orAHhzDCSVl7yHP9UEsX0DA_xbGbq-I\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"cacheKeyPrefix\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"xynolog.cache.\",\n    \"docs\": \"What a client keeps of a query, for one person, is kept under this followed by the knowledge base's id, a dot, the person's key as `lastEventIdKeyPrefix` makes it, a dot and the query's name: one `cacheDocument` for each query specs/src/client/refresh.json marks `persisted`. Nothing is kept for a token whose person the gateway has not named, and forgetting the knowledge base's stored sign-in, however it is forgotten, deletes the key of every kept query.\",\n    \"example\": {\n      \"kbId\": \"kb-a\",\n      \"did\": \"did:web:kb.example.org:users:jo%40example.org\",\n      \"query\": \"annotation\",\n      \"key\": \"xynolog.cache.kb-a.gqB898gk4Ww_orAHhzDCSVl7yHP9UEsX0DA_xbGbq-I.annotation\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"wholeKey\": {\n    \"key\": \"_\",\n    \"docs\": \"The key a kept query that is per nothing (a `queries` row of specs/src/client/refresh.json with no `per`) keeps its one entry under.\"\n  },\n  \"storedSession\": {\n    \"title\": \"StoredSession\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"What is kept of a sign-in: the tokens an issuer issued, the client they were issued to, and the issuer's endpoints a renewal and a sign-out need, learned once at sign-in so no session asks again. TOKENS, never a password. A stored value that lacks a member it requires is no session.\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"access\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The access token: short-lived, sent as a Bearer token.\"\n      },\n      \"refresh\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The refresh token: what renews the access token at the issuer without another sign-in.\"\n      },\n      \"clientId\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The client the tokens were issued to, which a renewal and a revocation name.\"\n      },\n      \"tokenEndpoint\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The issuer's token endpoint, where the refresh grant is made.\"\n      },\n      \"revocationEndpoint\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The issuer's revocation endpoint (RFC 7009), where a sign-out tells it to forget the refresh token. Absent when the issuer has none.\"\n      },\n      \"personKey\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Who the gateway said the sign-in's person is, as the key their caches and stream position are kept under (`lastEventIdKeyPrefix`), never the did itself. Written once the gateway names the person, on the sign-in whose token it was asked about; a renewal keeps it, a new sign-in starts without it, and forgetting the sign-in, however it is forgotten, reads it first to delete what is kept under it. Absent for a sign-in whose gateway has not yet named its person.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"access\", \"refresh\", \"clientId\", \"tokenEndpoint\"]\n  },\n  \"pendingAuthorization\": {\n    \"title\": \"PendingAuthorization\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"What a sign-in by a page redirect remembers across the trip to the issuer and back: the verifier and the state the issuer's response must match, where the person was connecting, what they believed they were connecting to, and the issuer's endpoints, so its completion asks nothing twice.\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"state\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"What the issuer's response must carry back to belong to this sign-in: random, as base64url.\"\n      },\n      \"verifier\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The PKCE code verifier (RFC 7636) the authorization code is exchanged with: random, as base64url.\"\n      },\n      \"redirectUri\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Where the issuer sends the person back to, named again when the code is exchanged.\"\n      },\n      \"target\": {\n        \"allOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/HttpEndpoint.json\" }],\n        \"description\": \"Where the person was connecting.\"\n      },\n      \"issuer\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"description\": \"The issuer the knowledge base trusts, and the endpoints of it a client uses.\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"issuer\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The issuer's identifier.\"\n          },\n          \"authorization\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The issuer's authorization endpoint, where the person is sent.\"\n          },\n          \"token\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The issuer's token endpoint, where the code is exchanged.\"\n          },\n          \"device\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The issuer's device authorization endpoint (RFC 8628). Absent when the issuer has none.\"\n          },\n          \"revocation\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The issuer's revocation endpoint (RFC 7009). Absent when the issuer has none.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"issuer\", \"authorization\", \"token\"]\n      },\n      \"kbId\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The registered knowledge base being signed in to again. Absent when it is none.\"\n      },\n      \"expectedDid\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The did of what the person believed they clicked, checked against the answer and never assumed. Absent when they named nothing.\"\n      },\n      \"expectedName\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The name of what the person believed they clicked. Absent when they named nothing.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"state\", \"verifier\", \"redirectUri\", \"target\", \"issuer\"]\n  },\n  \"openResource\": {\n    \"title\": \"OpenResource\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"A resource open in a knowledge base: which resource, the name it is shown by, when it was opened and its place among the others open there. A registry shows them by their places, and two in one place by when each was opened, first first.\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"id\": {\n        \"allOf\": [{ \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/ResourceId.json\" }],\n        \"description\": \"The resource.\"\n      },\n      \"name\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The name the resource is shown by.\"\n      },\n      \"openedAt\": {\n        \"type\": \"integer\",\n        \"minimum\": 0,\n        \"description\": \"When the resource was opened, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch. Opening it again while it is open changes neither this nor its place.\"\n      },\n      \"order\": {\n        \"type\": \"integer\",\n        \"minimum\": 0,\n        \"description\": \"The resource's place among those open in the knowledge base. One opened is given the place after the last taken, so a place freed by closing one is not given twice; a move gives each its place in the new order, counted from 0.\"\n      },\n      \"mediaType\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The resource's media type, which its icon is chosen by. Absent when it is not known.\"\n      },\n      \"storageUri\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Where the resource is in the knowledge base's working tree, as a URI (file://docs/overview.md). Absent when it is not known.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"openedAt\", \"order\"]\n  },\n  \"cacheDocument\": {\n    \"title\": \"CacheDocument\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"What a client keeps of one query: each key it was asked of, the value its answer gave, and when that value was received.\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"version\": {\n        \"const\": 1,\n        \"description\": \"The form of the document. A document of another version is read as none.\"\n      },\n      \"entries\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"description\": \"The query's kept keys. A document larger than `maxStoredBytesCount` (specs/src/client/timing.json) loses the entries received longest ago until it fits.\",\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"prefixItems\": [\n            { \"description\": \"The key: a resource's id for a query per resource, an annotation's id for one per annotation, `wholeKey` for one per nothing.\" },\n            { \"description\": \"The value: what the query's `value` in specs/src/client/refresh.json says its cache holds.\" },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"integer\",\n              \"minimum\": 0,\n              \"description\": \"When the value was received, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch. A value received again unchanged (its JSON text the text it was kept with) keeps the time it was first received.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"minItems\": 3,\n          \"maxItems\": 3\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\"version\", \"entries\"]\n  },\n  \"lastEventIds\": {\n    \"title\": \"LastEventIds\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"Where a knowledge base's stream was: for each scope, a resource's id, the id of the last recorded event delivered on it.\",\n    \"propertyNames\": { \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/ResourceId.json\" },\n    \"additionalProperties\": { \"$ref\": \"../components/schemas/PersistedEventId.json\" }\n  }\n}\n";
    internal const string Discovery = "{\n  \"title\": \"DiscoveryDocument\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"description\": \"The launcher's KB discovery document \\u2014 the schema authority for <stateDir>/discovery/kbs.json, which the Xynolog CLI (xynolog/cli) regenerates on every stack mutation and the Browser container mounts read-only at /discovery. NOT an API endpoint: a static document fetched same-origin by browsers (via the Browser's static server). An empty kbs list is meaningful (\\\"the launcher manages nothing right now\\\") and distinct from an absent file.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"version\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Document schema version. Consumers MUST check it and ignore documents they do not understand.\"\n    },\n    \"kbs\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"./DiscoveredKB.json\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Every KB the launcher currently manages, local and forwarded\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"version\",\n    \"kbs\"\n  ]\n}\n";
    internal const uint WindowsOffsetHigh = 0x40000000U;
    internal const string StoreFileName = "tokens.json";
    internal const string StoreLockName = "tokens.lock";
}
